#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171827 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "973cf948-eeb3-5c46-b0ac-ee0307a8043a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Line Integrals of Unity Over Polar Curves"}] :question/id #uuid "f6f11512-c37f-5922-b642-5290003b1d91" :question/math-academy-id "e-9492" :question/problem "Find a definite integral with respect to $\\theta$ that's equivalent to $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\,\\textrm d s$, where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=1-\\sin{\\theta}\\,$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi$, shown above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3354/Source/Images/51abfb11c3d6ee34e7a5825e34b8c9af.png)" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C$, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = L\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\textrm d s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm ds = \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2}\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as\n\n$$\nr = r(\\theta)\n$$\n\nfor\n\n$$\n\\theta_1 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\theta_2\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\nL= \\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2}\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\nr=1-\\sin{\\theta}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} = -\\cos{\\theta}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{C}ds &= ∫_{θ_{1}}^{θ_{2}}\\sqrt{r^{2} + (\\frac{dr}{dθ})^{2}}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{(1 - \\sin θ)^{2} + (-\\cos θ)^{2}}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{1 - 2\\sin θ + \\sin^{2} θ + \\cos^{2} θ}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{2 - 2\\sin θ}dθ \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2}∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{1 - \\sin θ}dθ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171828 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5777905c-e581-5454-bdbe-29878ad1237b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Line Integrals of Unity Over Polar Curves"}] :question/id #uuid "6753365e-9915-5be9-9a6d-d4c40b2caea0" :question/math-academy-id "e-9493" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\,\\textrm d s$, where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=2(1+\\sin\\theta)$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq {\\pi}$, shown above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3354/Source/Images/59d37d12b3beaf320cda903e9d7a14d4.png)" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C$, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = L\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\textrm d s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm ds = \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2}\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as\n\n$$\nr = r(\\theta)\n$$\n\nfor\n\n$$\n\\theta_1 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\theta_2\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\nL= \\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2}\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\nr=2(1+\\sin\\theta)\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} = 2\\cos{\\theta}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL &= ∫_{θ_{1}}^{θ_{2}}\\sqrt{r^{2} + (\\frac{dr}{dθ})^{2}}dθ \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{4(1 + \\sin θ)^{2} + 4(\\cos θ)^{2}}dθ \\\\\n&= 2∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{1 + 2\\sin θ + \\sin^{2} θ + \\cos^{2} θ}dθ \\\\\n&= 2∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{1 + 2\\sin θ + 1}dθ \\\\\n&= 2∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{2 + 2\\sin θ}dθ \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{2}∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{1 + \\sin θ}dθ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identities:\n\n$$\n\\sin^{2} (\\frac{θ}{2}) + \\cos^{2} (\\frac{θ}{2}) = 1, \\sin θ = 2\\sin (\\frac{θ}{2})\\cos (\\frac{θ}{2})\n$$\n\nRewriting our integral using the above identities, we can evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL &= 2\\sqrt{2}∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{1 + \\sin θ}dθ \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{2}∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{\\sin^{2} (\\frac{θ}{2}) + \\cos^{2} (\\frac{θ}{2}) + 2\\sin (\\frac{θ}{2})\\cos (\\frac{θ}{2})}dθ \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{2}∫_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{(\\sin (\\frac{θ}{2}) + \\cos (\\frac{θ}{2}))^{2}}dθ \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{2}∫_{0}^{π} \\mid \\sin (\\frac{θ}{2}) + \\cos (\\frac{θ}{2}) \\mid dθ \\\\\n&= 4\\sqrt{2}[- \\cos (\\frac{θ}{2}) + \\sin (\\frac{θ}{2})]_{0}^{π} \\\\\n&= 4\\sqrt{2}(-\\cos (\\frac{π}{2}) + \\sin (\\frac{π}{2})) - (-\\cos (0) + \\sin (0)) \\\\\n&= 4\\sqrt{2}((0 + 1) - (-1 + 0)) \\\\\n&= 8\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "973cf948-eeb3-5c46-b0ac-ee0307a8043a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Line Integrals of Unity Over Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a63d30ea-563a-5865-93f9-04c8be9b60b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{π/3}^{π}\\sqrt{4 - 5\\cos^{2} θ}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168524} {:answer/id #uuid "fae821cd-ebea-59d3-9c43-43a0a4868d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{π/3}^{π}\\sqrt{5 + 4\\cos^{2} θ}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168525} {:answer/id #uuid "682d112d-f8b5-5172-a439-4491c7e2c9ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{π/3}^{π}\\sqrt{1 - 2\\cos θ}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168526} {:answer/id #uuid "7626563e-3885-5849-bf0a-c7ff93c99c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{π/3}^{π}\\sqrt{1 - 2\\cos^{2} θ}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168527} {:answer/id #uuid "7c157a80-f241-5e4a-80e8-b43a6cd3a63e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{π/3}^{π}\\sqrt{5 - 4\\cos θ}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c157a80-f241-5e4a-80e8-b43a6cd3a63e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{π/3}^{π}\\sqrt{5 - 4\\cos θ}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168528} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6fb6796-187f-58b0-abc5-519ecbd5e76e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168523}] :question/id #uuid "2c8bb8d5-c684-5d53-8ebb-fc2e85b6f1e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-123355" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3354/Source/Images/q-123355.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to $∫_{C}ds$, where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r = 1 - 2\\cos θ$ for $\\frac{π}{3} \\le θ \\le π$, shown above?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "973cf948-eeb3-5c46-b0ac-ee0307a8043a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Line Integrals of Unity Over Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfa492a8-e07a-522a-bf45-34af18c7a267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π}\\sec^{2} θ\\tan^{2} θdθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168530} {:answer/id #uuid "1813a2d0-d5bd-52b4-99b5-efcb1d2a7640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π}\\sec^{3} θ\\sqrt{1 + \\tan^{2} θ}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168531} {:answer/id #uuid "2aba48aa-c769-5c6a-9e07-f0c67be25a4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{- π/2}^{π/2}\\sec^{3} θ\\sqrt{1 + 9\\tan^{2} θ}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168532} {:answer/id #uuid "55f60188-6938-5f92-aae8-dedef3328cd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{- π/2}^{π/2}\\sec^{3} θ\\sqrt{9 + \\tan^{2} θ}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168533} {:answer/id #uuid "5d3a3ab0-69fc-59cc-bc73-08e310482454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2∫_{0}^{π}\\sec^{3} θ\\sqrt{1 + \\sec^{2} θ}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2aba48aa-c769-5c6a-9e07-f0c67be25a4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{- π/2}^{π/2}\\sec^{3} θ\\sqrt{1 + 9\\tan^{2} θ}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168532} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4363fdf-f405-59b8-b8f3-f8bb7ba8806f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168529}] :question/id #uuid "f58568c3-ce47-5162-ad81-da8c754e43d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-123439" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $∫_{C}ds$, where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r = \\sec^{3} θ$ for $- π/2 \\le θ \\le π/2$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5777905c-e581-5454-bdbe-29878ad1237b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Line Integrals of Unity Over Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d623c90a-0ad7-53ed-885a-9969a8e11369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168536} {:answer/id #uuid "fca169d6-dd9e-555a-b9ec-7366d4c6fe64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168537} {:answer/id #uuid "19146a5b-799c-5a2f-81c5-df2b4f4e22a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168538} {:answer/id #uuid "33f9b7d4-7691-507e-8e83-b44ea5ae5578" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168539} {:answer/id #uuid "77c4bfbc-e7fe-58b1-8115-f2388b73dbef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d623c90a-0ad7-53ed-885a-9969a8e11369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168536} :answer-field/id #uuid "89528689-bacd-5edf-9c5c-5be78a32d2ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168535}] :question/id #uuid "474b9c27-587d-5510-bc2c-fbc91f7d6903" :question/math-academy-id "q-123623" :question/problem "Calculate $∫_{C}ds$, where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r = \\sec θ$ for $\\fra